  "question": {
    "text": "The electric field in an electromagnetic wave is given by $\\overrightarrow{\\mathrm{E}}=\\hat{i} 40 \\cos \\omega(\\mathrm{t}-z / \\mathrm{c}) \\mathrm{NC}^{-1}$. The magnetic field induction of this wave is (in SI unit) :",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "MvsI2",
      "text": "$\\overrightarrow{\\mathrm{B}}=\\hat{k} \\frac{40}{\\mathrm{C}} \\cos \\omega(\\mathrm{t}-z / \\mathrm{c})$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "3HtQw",
      "text": "$\\vec{B}=\\hat{j} 40 \\cos \\omega(t-z / c)$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "Z3C5Y",
      "text": "$\\overrightarrow{\\mathrm{B}}=\\hat{i} \\frac{40}{\\mathrm{C}} \\cos \\omega(\\mathrm{t}-z / \\mathrm{c})$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "0Hdch",
      "text": "$\\overrightarrow{\\mathrm{B}}=\\hat{j} \\frac{40}{\\mathrm{C}} \\cos \\omega(\\mathrm{t}-z / \\mathrm{c})$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": true
    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "$\\overrightarrow{\\mathrm{E}}=\\hat{\\mathrm{i}} 40 \\cos \\omega\\left(\\mathrm{t}-\\frac{\\mathrm{z}}{\\mathrm{c}}\\right)$\n$\\overrightarrow{\\mathrm{E}}$ is along $+\\mathrm{x}$ direction\n$\\overrightarrow{\\mathrm{v}}$ is along $+\\mathrm{z}$ direction\nSo direction of $\\vec{B}$ will be along +y and magnitude of $B$ will be $\\frac{E}{c}$\nSo answer is $\\frac{40}{c} \\cos \\omega\\left(t-\\frac{z}{c}\\right) \\hat{j}$",
    "image": null
  },
